[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=UDP Extract Data v1.0\\\\Companion to UDP Broadcast and Receive||1
  Cmn2=v1.3. One instance latches IP, MAC, UID,\\and raw Data from the||1
  Cmn3=last inbound packet that matches this instance's filter.\\\\Wire||1
  Cmn4=Received_IP / Received_MAC / Received_UID / Received_Data from the||1
  Cmn5=UDP\\module (same cue names). Do not wire Enable_FB.\\\\Filter:||1
  Cmn6=Match_IP, Match_MAC, and Match_UID (each with a serial override).
  Cmn7=\\Default for every match parameter is [SKIP] (do not use that field).
  Cmn8=\\Any combination of the three may be active; all active fields||1
  Cmn9=must match\\(AND). Exact, case-sensitive compare.\\\\At startup||1
  Cmn10=the locals take the parameters, then any override with length >||1
  Cmn11=0.\\CHANGE on an override sets that local to the override string||1
  Cmn12=as-is; an empty\\string means [SKIP] from then on (does not fall||1
  Cmn13=back to the parameter).\\\\UDP v1.3 clears then fills Received_*;||1
  Cmn14=this module waits 0.01 s after the\\last CHANGE so the snapshot||1
  Cmn15=is complete before matching.\\A non-match does not clear already||1
  Cmn16=latched outputs.\\\\In the SIMPL program, pulse UDP Retrigger on||1
  Cmn17=CHANGE Received_IP so a new\\talker gets this processor's announce||1
  Cmn18=back.\\\\Peer_UID is Received_UID from the matching packet (when||1
  Cmn19=the filter is IP or MAC).\\Peer_Data is the raw Received_Data from||1
  Cmn20=the matching packet.\\\\Drop one copy of this symbol per peer.\\
  Cmn21=\\-- VERSION HISTORY --\\v1.0  2026-09-09\\- Initial companion latch||1
  Cmn22=/ filter\\
[END]
